<metadata><name>Day 74 - Beth Gilhespy, John Appleton, Mshkiki Miikaansing, Hawthorn</name></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.958825" lon="-81.226168"><name>P Start/finish parking</name><desc>Bruce Trail Parking Lot: Off of Bruce Rd 9 in Barrow Bay, just south of West Shore Rd. Free</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.950640" lon="-81.222270"><name>P2 alternative parking</name><desc>BTC Parking Area on the east side of the road; emergency #2461 Bruce County Rd 9. Free. Joins the route near km 1.8 (0 m walk).</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.958814" lon="-81.226177"><name>J1</name><desc>J1: You pass the start again. Keep going on the white-blazed main Bruce Trail, heading south.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.951269" lon="-81.221888"><name>J2</name><desc>J2: Turn right onto the blue-blazed Hawthorn Side Trail, heading south. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your left.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.950675" lon="-81.222203"><name>J3</name><desc>J3: End of the Hawthorn Side Trail. There is trailhead parking here (BTC Parking Area on the east side of the road; emergency #2461 Bruce County Rd 9). Turn around and retrace your steps.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.952590" lon="-81.218572"><name>J4</name><desc>J4: Continue straight onto the blue-blazed John Appleton Side Trail, heading north-east. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your left.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.952839" lon="-81.210624"><name>J5</name><desc>J5: Turn right onto the blue-blazed Beth Gilhespy Side Trail, heading east. (the blue-blazed John Appleton Side Trail goes off on your left.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.958364" lon="-81.201655"><name>J6</name><desc>J6: Continue straight onto the white-blazed main Bruce Trail, heading west. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off behind you.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.954898" lon="-81.216527"><name>J7</name><desc>J7: Turn sharp left onto the blue-blazed John Appleton Side Trail, heading east. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off ahead.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
